      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-17T14:04:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there way to use OpenShift w/o projects? Or asked differently: can you create namespaces in OpenShift without creating a project as well or is the a 1:1 relationship between the two?",
      "parentUuid": "c06524cc_dfe0216b",
      "revId": "cf0dd456f36743341b2c0e24e1f1a7234ef0a5ba",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "575d119e_4127539c",
        "filename": "zuul/driver/kubernetes/kubernetesconnection.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-18T14:54:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe it\u0027s a permission.  So, typically, users would not have permissions to create namespaces, but would have perms to create project requests (which cause projects to be created; that\u0027s what we do here).  But there\u0027s a permission that would allow direct namespace creation (that\u0027s how the component that processes the project requests works).",
      "parentUuid": "c06524cc_dfe0216b",
      "revId": "cf0dd456f36743341b2c0e24e1f1a7234ef0a5ba",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58b32ef5_a1e40749",
        "filename": "zuul/driver/kubernetes/kubernetesconnection.py",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
